{
  "name": "Founder paid a vendor bill personally, company reimburses",
  "description": "The founder bought the domain on a personal card. The bill is the registrar's: its contract is with the vendor, and the bill posts the expense against 2110 payables for the vendor. The founder paying it is a second recording on the same vendor contract: pay_related settles the vendor's payable and credits 2135 Due to related parties for the founder (toPartyRole names who is owed), naming the founder's own card, an account registered with ownerPartyId from the last four digits on the receipt. Repaying the founder is recorded on the founder's own contract (its party is the founder): reimburse_related from the bank, bounded by everything the business owes them. If the founder instead contributes it, contribute_related on that contract moves it to their capital. Ask the founder which, once, and record the answer (asking-the-founder.md).",
